:9,"created_at":"2026-10-22T17:42:31Z","updated_at":"2026-10-22T17:42:31Z","browser_download_url":"https://github.com/base/base/releases/download/v1.5.1/basectl-v1.5.1-x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu.tar.gz.sha256"}],"tarball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/base/base/tarball/v1.5.1","zipball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/base/base/zipball/v1.5.1","body":"## What Changed\r\n\r\n> [!IMPORTANT]\r\n> **Base Mainnet**: Operators must upgrade to this release by November 5 at 18:00:00 UTC for the Denim hardfork. See [here](https://docs.base.org/upgrades/denim/overview) for more information.\r\n> **Base Sepolia**: Denim is already active on Base Sepolia, so there is no new activation in this release. Upgrading is recommended for the peer discovery fix and transaction pool performance improvements.\r\n>\r\n> The default batcher throttle thresholds have changed, and the DA backlog is now measured in estimated compressed bytes: `--throttle-start-threshold` from 1,000,000 to 120,000,000 and `--throttle-full-threshold` from 2,000,000 to 360,000,000. Batcher operators who set these flags explicitly should recalibrate them for the new unit.\r\n\r\n### base-reth-node\r\n- Denim support on Base Mainnet, activating November 5 at 18:00:00 UTC\r\n- Faster transaction pool: forwarded transaction batches are validated together against one state provider, sequential lanes are invalidated lazily, and validity conditions are partitioned after ingestion\r\n- New opt-in `--tx-forwarding-batched-insert` flag inserts forwarded transaction batches in one builder call (builders and sequencers must be upgraded before mempool nodes enable it)\r\n- Bug fixes and improvements\r\n\r\n### base-consensus\r\n- Denim support on Base Mainnet, activating November 5 at 18:00:00 UTC\r\n- Peers behind NAT can now join the discovery table\r\n- Bug fixes and improvements\r\n\r\n**Full Changelog**: https://github.com/base/base/compare/v1.5.0...v1.5.1"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/base/base/releases/4131